# KNOWN REGRESSION (issue #518).  Along with flow/rnr/mix2.buda, this is one
# of the two corpus vehicles the `band_span_charge` default flip costs: it now
# ends 3 overlaps / 16 unplaced bits instead of fully clean 0/0/0.  Same mix2
# design, same residual (bundle 61 seg 2), same root cause — the
# absolute-supply blind spot, where the width books say the spread bus fits
# but DetailedNUTS still needs real SIGNAL tracks at the placed position.
# Three repair attempts were measured and all lost corpus-wide; see
# docs/internal/band_span_charge.md.
#
# Uncomment before run_planner to restore the clean endpoint on this flow:
#set_planner_param band_span_charge 0
#
# Deliberately NOT applied: this is a corpus row, and silencing it would make
# the QoR guard stop reporting a known real regression.
#
# Selection-basis lever 3 composition vehicle (the refine_selection docs
# recipe, measured 2026-07-30): the PLAIN top-down mix2 pipeline (no healers)
# ends at 175 DNUTS opens / 16 NUTS overlaps on the reference x86 build; the
# end-of-flow recipe
#   refine_selection -> negotiate_congestion -> ripup_reroute -> refine_selection
# heals it to a fully clean check_design (0 opens / 0 overlaps, Success):
# refine's componentwise pre-shrink (175->84 opens, WL 67558->65480) hands the
# healers a much smaller problem, negotiate cracks the residual (84->32),
# ripup finishes to 0/0 (WL spent up to 69894 -- the healers' metrics don't
# track WL), and the trailing refine claws part of it back (69894->69621).
# The first refine doubles as a healer here BECAUSE the flow is healerless:
# its componentwise accept lets opens/overlap improvements through too.
source mix_tracks.buda
open_bdb mix2.bdb.sql
derive_busterms 2
add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
run_hier_bundler depth 2
generate_hier_topologies
run_planner hier 5 signal_tracks
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
refine_selection
negotiate_congestion
ripup_reroute
refine_selection
report_wl
check_design
exit
